l/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=154594#post154594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, thanks for sharing all the hard work!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aliveamongthedead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=154594#post154594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been trying to figure out why some of the V20 character sheets don't have the clan name at the top. They just have small boxes of various sizes. I tried getting the newest version of Adobe Reader, just to make sure it wasn't that. Anyone know why that's happening? The Malk one is the one that I'm trying to get, but when I checked around I saw it wasn't the only one that has that problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats very strange. I just checked my files and they seem ok, so I went to my site and loaded one up in the browser, and sure enough, weird boxes across the top. But, when I downloaded the file to my computer and opened it up, it was fine.<br /> <br /> So, I suspect it an issue with the browser not reading the font properly for that pdf for some reason. Very weird...but, since it's an issue with some and not all, I'd guess the acrobat browser plug-in is having issues decoding the font properly or something.<br /> <br /> So, if you right click the links and do a save-as and download it to your