k\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T05:37:35-07:00","id":728546,"title":"","content":"Now is that for both the visual design of the PDF as well as the actually turning it into a pdf file?<br /> <br /> Basically i'm looking to design my own sheet for a non OP rpg because the official sheet is really not printer friendly. Just trying to get an idea of how difficult this will be to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T13:05:03-07:00","id":729709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfsarkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=728546#post728546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now is that for both the visual design of the PDF as well as the actually turning it into a pdf file?<br /> <br /> Basically i'm looking to design my own sheet for a non OP rpg because the official sheet is really not printer friendly. Just trying to get an idea of how difficult this will be to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less difficult on it's own and more very very fussy in terms of manipulation and tools tend to be expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T16:24:20-07:00","id":730297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfsarkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=728546#post728546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now is that for both the visual design of the PDF as well as the actually turning it into a pdf file?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The sheets I make are pdf's from start to finish. I'll basically take a blank pdf page and then add all the elements line by line and graphic by graphic. It can be a bit of a pain sometimes(especially with the newer versions), but the end result is usually pretty good.<br /> <br /> Acrobat isn't the most user friendly program though, and it's taken me years to work around it's quirks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of course, I'm used to it now...but it can still be frustrating at times. But, the more you use it the easier it gets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfsarkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=728546#post728546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically i'm looking to design my own sheet for a non OP rpg because the official sheet is really not printer friendly. Just trying to get an idea of how difficult this will be to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thats cool. Well, if you decide to use Acrobat I can always give you some pointers...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=729709#post729709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's less difficult on it's own and more very very fussy in terms of manipulation and tools tend to be expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! And yea, Acrobat can be pretty expensive, again, especially the newer versions..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:47:14-07:00","id":732627,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help you guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T11:50:19-07:00","id":732727,"title":"","content":"Acrobat costs $40-$60/month now for information. As an alternative there is the tools from Foxit (Phantom IIRC) which are fairly cheap but more limited. I've used it in the past to make personalized modded stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:27:13-07:00","id":732815,"title":"","content":"As a designer of character sheets myself, having used a variety of tools (MS paint, Photoshop, inDesign and Illustrator being the ones I found to work best at the time I was using them, which I've listed chronologically) I would suggest checking out a few programs to find one that just &quot;clicks&quot; for you.<br /> <br /> I say that because back in the day Mr. Gone commented with surprise that I had done a sheet with Paint, and when he mentioned he uses Acrobat Pro I tried it out and just couldn't wrap my head around how it was even possible (it was years ago now, but I recall starting by trying to replicate a sheet I made in Paint and couldn't even get my head around how to put a skill list, lines, and dots where I wanted it to be).<br /> <br /> Overall, I find I prefer making any art assets in Illustrator (another vector art program could work, I haven't tried any myself though because Inkscape won't even run when I install it) and assembling the art plus text with inDesign, unless the sheet doesn't have much variety in text (font and size combos, which are easy to program in and reuse in inDesign) in which case I stick with Illustrator for everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:01:24-07:00","id":733322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfsarkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=732627#post732627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the help you guys!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're very welcome! Hope it helps a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=732727#post732727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acrobat costs $40-$60/month now for information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not sure what I think of subscription based software...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=732727#post732727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an alternative there is the tools from Foxit (Phantom IIRC) which are fairly cheap but more limited. I've used it in the past to make personalized modded stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only used Foxit in a limited fashion, and only the reader really. I keep thinking I should check out some of the full versions, but I haven't gotten around to it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=732815#post732815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a designer of character sheets myself, having used a variety of tools (MS paint, Photoshop, inDesign and Illustrator being the ones I found to work best at the time I was using them, which I've listed chronologically) I would suggest checking out a few programs to find one that just &quot;clicks&quot; for you.<br /> <br /> I say that because back in the day Mr. Gone commented with surprise that I had done a sheet with Paint, and when he mentioned he uses Acrobat Pro I tried it out and just couldn't wrap my head around how it was even possible (it was years ago now, but I recall starting by trying to replicate a sheet I made in Paint and couldn't even get my head around how to put a skill list, lines, and dots where I wanted it to be).<br /> <br /> Overall, I find I prefer making any art assets in Illustrator (another vector art program could work, I haven't tried any myself though because Inkscape won't even run when I install it) and assembling the art plus text with inDesign, unless the sheet doesn't have much variety in text (font and size combos, which are easy to program in and reuse in inDesign) in which case I stick with Illustrator for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought about trying Illustrator and InDesign before, but again, just haven't gotten around to it sadly. Theres going to come a day when I'm not going to be able to use my old version of Acrobat, and I'm not sure what I'm going to do...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:00:52-07:00","id":739916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=733322#post733322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought about trying Illustrator and InDesign before, but again, just haven't gotten around to it sadly. Theres going to come a day when I'm not going to be able to use my old version of Acrobat, and I'm not sure what I'm going to do...</div> </div> </div> </div>InDesign has always felt very intuitive to me. The only &quot;help&quot; I needed in order to get it doing what I needed was to check out what things where in which menu bar menu, find the drop down menu that says things like &quot;essentials&quot; and &quot;book&quot; and select book (which put the majority of tools I needed in plain view), and then later look up how to insert a graphic because I was expected that function to be in the Edit or Object menus when it is actually under the (probably intended to be intuitive) File menu and is called &quot;place&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, and I don't know if other programs allow the same type of thing, but it lets you select &quot;paper&quot; as the fill for drawn shapes so you can lay a paper-filled rectangle over the ragged ends of lines you want to all end at the same point instead of futzing with some kind of layer-mask system that always manages to work differently in every single program I use so I can never keep straight how to mask the right part the first time (and some don't have an easy invert option).<br /> <br /> So if the day comes along that you can no longer use &quot;old reliable&quot;, I suggest giving it a try - especially now that Adobe has changed their sales style to a relatively affordable monthly fee rather than the hundreds-of-dollars-even-with-student-discount-of-dramatic-percentage buy-in and upgrade prices (which if they'd have implemented a couple years ago, I might not currently be so strapped for fun-budget as to not be able to afford to upgrade to the 'creative cloud').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T04:35:37-07:00","id":741309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=739916#post739916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">InDesign has always felt very intuitive to me. The only &quot;help&quot; I needed in order to get it doing what I needed was to check out what things where in which menu bar menu, find the drop down menu that says things like &quot;essentials&quot; and &quot;book&quot; and select book (which put the majority of tools I needed in plain view), and then later look up how to insert a graphic because I was expected that function to be in the Edit or Object menus when it is actually under the (probably intended to be intuitive) File menu and is called &quot;place&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, and I don't know if other programs allow the same type of thing, but it lets you select &quot;paper&quot; as the fill for drawn shapes so you can lay a paper-filled rectangle over the ragged ends of lines you want to all end at the same point instead of futzing with some kind of layer-mask system that always manages to work differently in every single program I use so I can never keep straight how to mask the right part the first time (and some don't have an easy invert option).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting. I may have to check it out sometime and play around with it. I've been using this version of Acrobat for like 12 or more years now, it'll be weird to switch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=739916#post739916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the day comes along that you can no longer use &quot;old reliable&quot;, I suggest giving it a try - especially now that Adobe has changed their sales style to a relatively affordable monthly fee rather than the hundreds-of-dollars-even-with-student-discount-of-dramatic-percentage buy-in and upgrade prices (which if they'd have implemented a couple years ago, I might not currently be so strapped for fun-budget as to not be able to afford to upgrade to the 'creative cloud').</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, not sure what I think about it. But, yea, I guess I can see how it'd be cheaper for people to be able to use it now with the monthly fee. I just wish it'd be cheaper before... Plus, I wonder how the fee's shake out in the end? Is it really cheaper, or does it just seem cheaper because you're paying month to month? Hmm...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T10:28:37-07:00","id":742181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=741309#post741309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, not sure what I think about it. But, yea, I guess I can see how it'd be cheaper for people to be able to use it now with the monthly fee. I just wish it'd be cheaper before... Plus, I wonder how the fee's shake out in the end? Is it really cheaper, or does it just seem cheaper because you're paying month to month? Hmm...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Compared to the pricing of buying a full creative suite and then upgrading every time a new creative suite comes out, which has typically been every 2-3 years lately (like CS4-6 did prior to going to &quot;the cloud&quot;), the pricing of ~$50 per month is a discount even over the student discounted price I payed for getting CS4 and upgrading to CS5 (and then deciding CS6 was not within my budget) because dividing the ~$2760 I spent over just the 18 months from CS4 launch to CS5 launch + 1 month comes out to ~$145 per month.<br /> <br /> Of course, in order for that pricing to keep looking like a discount, the programs are going to have to keep having noteworthy improvements at least every few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T06:47:53-07:00","id":744338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=742181#post742181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compared to the pricing of buying a full creative suite and then upgrading every time a new creative suite comes out, which has typically been every 2-3 years lately (like CS4-6 did prior to going to &quot;the cloud&quot;), the pricing of ~$50 per month is a discount even over the student discounted price I payed for getting CS4 and upgrading to CS5 (and then deciding CS6 was not within my budget) because dividing the ~$2760 I spent over just the 18 months from CS4 launch to CS5 launch + 1 month comes out to ~$145 per month.<br /> <br /> Of course, in order for that pricing to keep looking like a discount, the programs are going to have to keep having noteworthy improvements at least every few years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a pretty good point. I guess it does shake out for the better.<br /> <br /> Of course, I will say that for the way I use Acrobat, each new version has made it more difficult, hence why I'm still using version 5. It does exactly what I need it to and doesn't act too wonky. Though, I'm pretty sure it in a way that it was never intended. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T15:27:17-07:00","id":745251,"title":"","content":"Greetings. I am a small fan of your work and I've come asking if you'd be interested in providing a character sheet for a fan splat called Dragon the Inheritance, not to be confused with Embers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?404998-nWoD-fansplat-Dragon-the-Inheritance\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...he-Inheritance</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I am a contributer for the project and I would like to have an editable character sheet for it.<br /> <br /> Would you be interested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:35:27-08:00","id":746681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35750-mrgone-s-character-sheets?p=745251#post745251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings. I am a small fan of your work and I've come asking if you'd be interested in providing a character sheet for a fan splat called Dragon the Inheritance, not to be confused with Embers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?404998-nWoD-fansplat-Dragon-the-Inheritance\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...he-Inheritance</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I am a contributer for the project and I would like to have an editable character sheet for it.<br /> <br /> Would you be interested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello. Glad to hear you like my work! Sure, I might be interested in helping. Just send me an email or PM and we'll see what we can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone